# Implementation Plan: Branch 1 (feat/core-infrastructure)

This plan outlines the foundational core architecture for the FastAPI backend, including environment configuration, custom exceptions (with Indonesian frontend-facing messages), basic logging and security utilities, asynchronous database connection setup, and initial Alembic configuration for database migrations.

## Implementation Stages & Commit Messages

The execution will be divided into 4 logical stages with separate commits (Commit messages in English, API error messages in Indonesian):

### Stage 1: Core Configuration and Custom Exceptions
**Commit Message:** `feat: add core configuration and custom exceptions`

#### [NEW] [config.py](file:///d:/KEISHA/Fasilkom/BYTESFEST/blusukan-be/app/core/config.py)
Implements the `Settings` class using `pydantic-settings` to manage environment variables (DATABASE_URL, SUPABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, etc.).
#### [NEW] [exceptions.py](file:///d:/KEISHA/Fasilkom/BYTESFEST/blusukan-be/app/core/exceptions.py)
Defines custom exception classes with HTTP status codes and specific `Error Code Strings`. The human-readable messages returned to the frontend will be in Indonesian:
- `OTPExpiredException` (400, `OTP_EXPIRED`) -> "Kode OTP sudah kedaluwarsa."
- `OTPRateLimitException` (429, `OTP_RATE_LIMIT`) -> "Terlalu banyak percobaan OTP. Silakan coba lagi nanti."
- `InvalidLocationException` (400, `INVALID_LOCATION`) -> "Lokasi tidak valid."
- `InsufficientBudgetException` (400, `INSUFFICIENT_BUDGET`) -> "Saldo atau budget tidak mencukupi."
- `PromoExpiredException` (400, `PROMO_EXPIRED`) -> "Promo sudah kedaluwarsa."
- `MerchantOwnershipException` (403, `FORBIDDEN_NOT_OWNER`) -> "Anda tidak memiliki akses ke merchant ini."
- `DuplicateStampException` (409, `STAMP_ALREADY_AWARDED`) -> "Stamp sudah diberikan sebelumnya."
- `TokenReuseDetectedException` (401, `TOKEN_REUSE_DETECTED`) -> "Penggunaan ulang token terdeteksi."
- `IngestLimitReachedException` (429, `INGEST_LIMIT_REACHED`) -> "Batas limit tercapai."

